+// coop-gatelost (Jep): transient chunks (each frame slot's vertices, indices and constant records, written by the CPU) use
+// host memory unless KZ_TRANSIENT_MEMORY is "device" (device-local host-visible memory, Kazarov's own default). On PC-01's
+// RTX 4070 Ti (ReBAR: a 11994 MiB device-local host-visible heap) x-dungeon-prompt-gatestays lost the device after the exit
+// gate's split (vkQueueSubmit2 -4) in 2 of 5 runs on the device path and 0 of 10 in host memory; no misuse was found
+// (validation with GPU-AV 0, every immediate mesh's indices inside its vertices). PC-02's GTX 1080 (no ReBAR: a 214 MiB
+// heap) never lost it either way. Which memory the chunks take is said once, at the first chunk.
